                <pb facs="0248" n="238" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg238"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.5151/638: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Buenos Aires</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Burdett</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-03-05T10:00:00-04:00">March 5, 1937—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 5—9:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Because of representations made by the Government-owned oil company, the
                    Argentine Government has decided to grant between 5½ and 6 million pesos of
                    official dollar exchange to importers of American crude petroleum in 1937. Have
                    informed the Embassy.</p>
                <p>Air mail report follows.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Burdett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
